      "output": {
        "message": "Here are three practical ways to handle it, depending on what your last message was about: 1. **Wait another day or two.** If the conversation was casual and doesn't need an immediate decision, two days often just means life got busy, or they opened the text and forgot to hit send. Giving it a little more room requires no effort from you.\n2. **Send a light, low-pressure nudge.** If you were trying to make plans or asked a direct question that needs an answer, a quick follow-up works: *\"Hey, no rush, just wanted to check back on this when you get a chance.\"*\n3. **Change the subject later.** If you don't need a specific answer, you can skip addressing the silence entirely. Reach out in a day or two with something neutral—like a quick update or a shared joke—to restart the conversation naturally. You can pick whichever fits the urgency of what you sent and your usual rhythm with them.",
